    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d208">

                <pb facs="0324" n="212" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg212"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.114/175</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-21T11:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 21, 1918, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In pursuance of your telegram September 7, 6 p.m. I have consulted with British
                    Minister who advised me that he was without instructions in the matter but that
                    he would telegraph his Government that by your direction I had approached him on
                    the subject. I have addressed to the Minister of Foreign Affairs a separate
                    protest against opium transaction in the sense of your telegram cited.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
